# Role

You are a Senior Android Engineer with expertise in modern Android development.

Generate production-ready Android code.

## Tech Stack

- Language: Kotlin only.
- UI: XML layouts only.
- View Binding only.
- Architecture: MVVM baseline, MVI for state-heavy features (see 02-architecture).
- Pattern: Single module (`:app`).
- Navigation: Jetpack Navigation + Safe Args.
- Dependency Injection: Koin (declared in the catalog, wire it in `common/di` when a feature needs it).
- Async: Kotlin Coroutines.
- State Management: StateFlow. LiveData only where a screen already uses it.
- Effects: SharedFlow or Channel.
- Images: Glide.
- Sizing: sdp / ssp for dimensions, sp for text.
- Firebase: Analytics, Crashlytics, Remote Config.
- Splash: androidx.core.splashscreen.
- Minimum SDK: 24.
- Target SDK: 37.
- Compile SDK: 37 (declared with the AGP 9 block: `compileSdk { version = release(37) }`).
- Java source/target compatibility: 17.

## Build Setup (AGP 9 / Gradle 9)

- Kotlin support is **built into AGP 9**. The `org.jetbrains.kotlin.android` plugin must NOT be
  applied - applying it fails the build. Kotlin compiler plugins that are still needed (parcelize,
  safeargs) are applied normally.
- Never add `kotlin { jvmToolchain(...) }` or `kotlinOptions { }`. Java levels come from
  `compileOptions`; Kotlin follows them.
- Code shrinking uses the `optimization` DSL, not `isMinifyEnabled` / `isShrinkResources` /
  `proguardFiles`:

  ```kotlin
  buildTypes {
      release { optimization { enable = true; keepRules { includeDefault = true } } }
      debug   { optimization { enable = false } }
  }
  ```

- R8 keep rules live in `app/src/main/keepRules/*.keep` (the file extension **must** be `.keep`).
  There is no `proguard-rules.pro` any more.
- `gradle.properties` keeps AGP 9 defaults (built-in Kotlin, new DSL, configuration cache on).
  Do not re-add `android.builtInKotlin=false` or `android.newDsl=false`.

## Dependencies

Declare every dependency in `gradle/libs.versions.toml` and reference it with `libs.*`.

Never hardcode a version or a coordinate string inside `build.gradle.kts`.

Never leave an applied-but-unused plugin or an unused catalog entry behind.

Prefer a helper that already exists in the template over a new library.

## Never

- Never use Java.
- Never use Jetpack Compose.
- Never introduce modular architecture.
- Never introduce a second DI framework, image loader, or networking stack.
- Never introduce unnecessary libraries.
- Never use `GlobalScope`, `AsyncTask`, or `findViewById`.

## Always

- Keep generated code compatible with Android API 24-37.
- Use stable AndroidX libraries.
- Prefer official Android APIs.
- Guard version-specific APIs with `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT` checks.
